  <sharedRules>
    <rule id="4763-8b0b-b92e-f675" name="Christian Spanish (AoA2) - List Notes" publicationId="fcb9-17be-94c2-bcfc" hidden="false">
      <description>ARMIES OF ANTIQUITY v2 #62 (unofficial, Martin Gibbins). After the Arab invasions, the Visigothic kingdom was reduced to a rump of statelets in the North of Spain. Against the odds, they survived and eventually thrived, fighting continually against each other and their Arab opponents and gradually regaining territory, a process which gained momentum after 1100 and resulted in the reconquest of the majority of Spain by 1250. The list can be used to create early, middle (1040 to 1100) and late variants of the army. 

ARMY COMPOSITIONS (pick one in the Army composition list):
[Christian Spanish - Early (711-1039)]
  Allies and Mercenaries: up to 25%
  Cavalry: up to 50%
  Characters: up to 25%
  Infantry: up to 50%
  Characters: Up to 25% Cavalry: Up to 50%. May not take Noble cavalry, heavy armour or military orders Infantry: Up to 50%. May not take crossbows. Allies &amp; Mercenaries: Up to 25% The army may have allies from the relevant period of the Al-Andalus and Granada list.
[Christian Spanish - Late (1101-1250)]
  Allies and Mercenaries: up to 25%
  Cavalry: up to 50%
  Characters: up to 25%
  Infantry: up to 50%
  Characters: Up to 25%. May ride warhorses (+16) and may take barding (+4) and lance (+6). Cavalry: Up to 50%. Noble cavalry may take barding (+4). Militia cavalry and Noble cavalry may have lance (+3). Infantry: Up to 50% Allies &amp; Mercenaries: Up to 25%
[Christian Spanish - Middle (1040–1100)]
  Allies and Mercenaries: up to 25%
  Cavalry: up to 50%
  Characters: up to 25%
  Infantry: up to 50%
  Characters: Up to 25%. May ride warhorses (+16). Cavalry: Up to 50%. May not take military orders. Infantry: Up to 50%. May take only one unit of crossbowmen. Allies &amp; Mercenaries: Up to 25% The army may have allies from the relevant period of the Al-Andalus and Granada list.</description>
    </rule>
  </sharedRules>
</catalogue>
